 34MG c  2014Mi09: a 63-MeV/nucleon {+48}Ca primary beam was accelerated by the 
 34MG2c  RIKEN RFQ-RILAC-CSM-RRC accelerator complex. Secondary beams containing
 34MG3c  {+34}Mg were produced by fragmentation of the primary beam on {+181}Ta 
 34MG4c  and enriched {+64}Ni targets, separated by the RIPS fragment separator,
 34MG5c  annd bombarded the liquid hydrogen secondary target at 51.1            
 34MG6c  MeV/nucleon. The scattered particles were analyzed by the TOMBEE       
 34MG7c  spectrometer and detected using a |DE-E telescope of a silicon detector
 34MG8c  and a NaI(Tl) detector. The |g rays from the excited states populated  
 34MG9c  by inelastic scattering were detected by the DALI2 array of 160 NaI(Tl)
 34MGAc  detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, |g yields,            
 34MGBc  ({+34}Mg)|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, cross sections for    
 34MGCc  population of excited states, deformation lengths, and |b{-2}          
 34MGDc  deformation parameters. Compared with SDPF-M shell-model calculations. 
 34MG c  2006El03: a 94-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ar primary beam was transported to a   
 34MG2c  {+181}Ta primary target. Tge secondary beams of 30Na, 31Na, {+33}Mg,   
 34MG3c  and {+34}Mg were separated by the RIPS fragment separator and bombarded
 34MG4c  a liquid hydrogen target at a mean energy of 50 MeV/nucleon. The       
 34MG5c  reaction products were detected and identified by a parallel-plate     
 34MG6c  avalanche counter (PPAC) and a silicon detector telescope. The         
 34MG7c  deexciting |g rays emitted by the inelastically scattered nuclei were  
 34MG8c  detected by the DALI2 setup consisting of 146 NaI(Tl) detectors.       
 34MG9c  Deduced mass deformation and neutron deformation parameters.           
